== Issues ==
{{issue list|Cactus|Cacti}}

== Trivia ==
* Cacti can be placed in 1 block deep water, provided they are placed on sand, and they grow if they break the surface.
* Cacti can be placed next to [[sapling]]s, but the cactus breaks when the tree grows.
* [[Endermen]] can move and place cacti, increasing the cactus population in [[desert]]s by moving cactus blocks as they grow.
* [[Sign]]s and [[painting]]s can be placed on the sides of cacti and behave as non-blocks, making them cause damage even though they are covering cacti.
* It is possible for cacti to generate on blocks other than sand due to [[generated structures|terrain generation]]; refer to the gallery for examples.
* The pre-[[Texture Update]] side and bottom textures is actually a recolor of the pre-Texture Update [[log]]. This can be easily seen if you increase the contrast on the Alpha 1.0.6 textures.
* Dying from touching a cactus displays "''<player>'' was pricked to death" in the chat messages.
* Blocks can be placed on top of a cactus, including other cactus blocks.
* It is possible to place [[redstone]] next to a cactus block without destroying it.
* A 20 block tall cactus can be found on the seed 43931985876593125 at coordinates (-9711824 , ~ , 7726416) and more recently a 22 block tall one on seed 11343195073417814 at coordinates (14955936 , ~ , -3750655) and even a 23 block tall one on the seed 184693195438010998 and coordinates (16274576 ~ 10230656). All these seeds, found by the Minecraft@home research project, work on ''Java Edition'' 1.14.4.<ref>{{Tweet|minecraftathome|1275401340731232256|With data generated from volunteer computers on our BOINC network, the tallest known cactus in #Minecraft was discovered yesterday at the 20 blocks high.<br><br>Seed: 43931985876593125<br>Position: -9711824 7726416}}</ref>
* Top snow can be placed next to cacti without breaking the cacti, no matter how many top snow layers stack.

